# SFT execution status v0.95

2026-09-16. The Source CI diagnostic recovered 15 observed, parameter-free failed
test identifiers in two files. This list is not claimed exhaustive. The one-shot
read on 2026-09-15 used two GETs and 99,267 bytes, below 128 KiB; no raw log,
exception message or parameter was retained. The authorization is consumed.

## Local fix completed

The two synthetic test contexts depended on the surrounding process's real
Python thread count. The runner's 25 old tests pass alone, but adding one owned
background thread reproduces guard-preemption failures. The generator's nominal
mocked-runtime test also changes from passing to `runtime_rejected` with a live
background thread. Actual remote thread state was not retained, so this is a
reproduced defect consistent with the failed identifiers, not a claim that every
remote failure cause has been proven.

Only the two test files were changed. They now replace their module-under-test's
`threading` reference with an explicit synthetic count, while retaining real
current/main thread identity functions. No global threading function or
production runtime guard was changed. Five added regressions cover modeled
extra-thread rejection, off-main rejection, and unrelated owned threads.

## Verification

- 46 tests passed on each of Python 3.11.15 and 3.13.7, both with and without an
  owned background thread: four successful runs, no skips or expected failures.
- 63 CI scope/workflow guard tests passed. The frozen Source partition still
  verifies all 423 bound files and preserves its 327 private entries.
- Production file hashes are unchanged; independent diff review found no blocker;
  `git diff --check` passed. Current hashes still match the tested files on resume.
- Ruff and the exact Ubuntu/Python 3.12 CI environment were not available locally.
  No packages were downloaded to fill those gaps.

## Remaining boundary

The fix is local, uncommitted and unpushed. No workflow, routing or test-selection
policy was changed; no test was removed, skipped or marked expected-failure.
Historical reports, plans and started markers remain unchanged. Historical test
bytes remain at commit `6585a1e073a6a5302630ed63a3c1a3d81adda429`; old native
qualification plans are not being silently rebound to the edited tests. A future
qualification successor must explicitly bind their new hashes and counts.

No additional remote read, CI/native rerun, GPU use, checkpoint import or training
occurred on resume. Source CI still requires remote verification after approved
publication. The earlier native qualification failure remains separately open;
its attempt is consumed. Gate 5 is not complete.

Evidence: `evidence/lumi-4b-sft-source-thread-context-fix-v0.1.json` and
`evidence/lumi-4b-sft-source-failure-names-v0.1.json`.
